# {{.Name}}

A production-grade, OpenAI-compatible Go LLM backend, generated by
**[llmberth](https://github.com/THY17308111153/llmberth)** — and fully owned
by you: zero runtime dependency on the generator, all source in this repo.

```
client (any OpenAI SDK / bundled UI)
   │  Authorization: Bearer lbt_live_…
   ▼
app (chi) ── auth ▸ rate limit ▸ budget ▸ provider ──▶ {{.Provider.DisplayName}}
   │
   ├─ Postgres (internal network; usage ledger, keys, audit)
   └─ admin API on 127.0.0.1:{{.Manifest.Services.App.AdminPort}} (llmberth CLI only)
```

## What's inside

- **OpenAI-compatible API** — `POST /v1/chat/completions` (stream & non-stream);
  any OpenAI SDK works by changing the base URL.
- **Usage ledger** — per-request token accounting; costs are **estimates**
  (price table: `internal/cost/models.yaml`), exposed via `X-LLM-Cost-Usd`.
- **API keys** — `lbt_live_…`, stored hashed (SHA-256) + 8-char prefix,
  per-key rate limit and budget, instant revocation via the loopback admin API.
- **Audit log** — every management action appended to `audit_log`.
- **Bundled UI** (single-page): chat frontend, strict CSP.
- **Provider**: {{.Provider.DisplayName}}{{if .Provider.NeedsAPIKey}} — set
  `{{.Provider.APIKeyEnv}}` in `.env`.{{else}} — no upstream API key needed{{end}}.

## Quick start

```bash
# 1. fill in .env (init already wrote ADMIN_TOKEN + POSTGRES_PASSWORD)
$EDITOR .env

# 2. start the stack (postgres + app; ports published to 127.0.0.1 only)
docker compose up -d --wait

# 3. create your first key via the admin API (loopback only)
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:{{.Manifest.Services.App.AdminPort}}/admin/keys \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(cat .llmberth-admin-token)" \
  -d '{"name":"first-key"}'
# → {"id":…, "key":"lbt_live_…", "warning":"store this key now — it is never displayed again"}

# 4. chat
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:{{.Manifest.Services.App.Port}}/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer lbt_live_YOUR_KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"{{.Provider.DefaultModel}}","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hello"}]}'
```

Any OpenAI SDK works with `base_url = http://127.0.0.1:{{.Manifest.Services.App.Port}}/v1`.

## Day-2 operations

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| logs | `docker compose logs -f app` |
| stop | `docker compose down` |
| keys (list/revoke) | admin API `GET/POST /admin/keys…` (Bearer `$(cat .llmberth-admin-token)`) |
| usage | `GET /admin/usage?by=model&since=…` |
| tests | `make test` (fake provider — no network, no keys) |

## Security defaults

- Admin API: loopback only + bearer token, fail closed.
- Postgres: internal network, host port published to 127.0.0.1 only.
- Keys: hashed at rest, constant-time comparison, revoked keys rejected on
  the very next request.
- Logs: message bodies are never logged (`LOG_MESSAGES=1` opts in to DB
  persistence only).
- Upstream: base_url allowlist (SSRF guard).
- Budgets: global monthly + per-key; exhausted → `429` with
  `reason=budget_exhausted`.

Costs shown anywhere (headers, admin API) are **estimates** from
`internal/cost/models.yaml` — always labeled as such.

